Z||000000||8Ball||08-08-2001||11:47 PM||||Ok well I went to go look at the 87 GT today.<BR>First thing it wasn't a GT it is an 87 2M6<BR>Still nice, The notch back will be good for the 89 conversion.<P>Ok here are the good things about it.<BR>1.No rust anywhere I could find. not even in the trunk.<BR>2.It has a strong V6, no knocks pings or leaks. And plenty of punch.<BR>3.It has never been wrecked. I checked the vin.<BR>4.The Interior is descent the usual tears.<BR>5.It is 800 dollars.<BR>6.Power Windows, tilt steering, sunroof<BR>7.Fun as heck to drive!!!!<P>The not so good things about it.<BR>1.Needs inner tie rod<BR>2.Headlights don't come up, the drivers side headlight motor had to be disconnected cause it keeps running.<BR>3.the paint is awful<BR>4.the body needs work small cracks and scratches and will need a new hood as it is pitted pretty bad,<BR>5.The gas seems to hesitate when you first start it up. Can press it to the floor and nothing will happen for about 1.5 seconds, but after that one time it is ok.<BR>6.Smokes just a little on start-up. I assume valve guides, no biggie.<BR>7.Passenger side front fender has a small hole in it about the size of a quarter, again no biggie<BR>8. LUGGAGE RACK<BR>9. decklid lock drilled out<P>Well that is all I can think of atm Please let me know what you think.<BR>If all works out I could prolly get it monday<P>Randy<P>Oh yea forgot to mention.. someone took off the air cond. compressor<p>[This message has been edited by 8Ball (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
